{"system": "no_memory", "input": "You are an expert medical diagnostician. Based on the patient's symptoms, provide a diagnosis.\n\nPossible diagnoses include: drug reaction, allergy, chicken pox, diabetes, psoriasis, hypertension, cervical spondylosis, bronchial asthma, varicose veins, malaria, dengue, arthritis, impetigo, fungal infection, common cold, gastroesophageal reflux disease, urinary tract infection, typhoid, pneumonia, peptic ulcer disease, jaundice, migraine.\n\nPlease analyze the symptoms step by step, then provide your final diagnosis in the format:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diagnosis_name[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\nFor example:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diabetes[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\n\n## Patient Symptoms\nI've been feeling really hot and sweaty, and I've been throwing up. I've also been shivering and my skin is really itchy. I have a headache and my muscles hurt.\n\nPlease provide your reasoning and final diagnosis.", "prediction": "[DIAGNOSIS]suspected malaria (requires urgent testing)[/DIAGNOSIS]", "ground_truth": "malaria", "was_correct": false, "prompt_len": 1042, "context_len": 191, "prompt_text": "Answer the following question.\n\nYou are an expert medical diagnostician. Based on the patient's symptoms, provide a diagnosis.\n\nPossible diagnoses include: drug reaction, allergy, chicken pox, diabetes, psoriasis, hypertension, cervical spondylosis, bronchial asthma, varicose veins, malaria, dengue, arthritis, impetigo, fungal infection, common cold, gastroesophageal reflux disease, urinary tract infection, typhoid, pneumonia, peptic ulcer disease, jaundice, migraine.\n\nPlease analyze the symptoms step by step, then provide your final diagnosis in the format:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diagnosis_name[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\nFor example:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diabetes[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\n\n## Patient Symptoms\nI've been feeling really hot and sweaty, and I've been throwing up. I've also been shivering and my skin is really itchy. I have a headache and my muscles hurt.\n\nPlease provide your reasoning and final diagnosis.\n\n**Answer in this exact JSON format:**\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"[Your chain of thought / reasoning process]\",\n  \"final_answer\": \"[Your concise final answer here]\"\n}\n", "trace_id": "0059fcf0866e"}
{"system": "class_signature_memory", "input": "You are an expert medical diagnostician. Based on the patient's symptoms, provide a diagnosis.\n\nPossible diagnoses include: drug reaction, allergy, chicken pox, diabetes, psoriasis, hypertension, cervical spondylosis, bronchial asthma, varicose veins, malaria, dengue, arthritis, impetigo, fungal infection, common cold, gastroesophageal reflux disease, urinary tract infection, typhoid, pneumonia, peptic ulcer disease, jaundice, migraine.\n\nPlease analyze the symptoms step by step, then provide your final diagnosis in the format:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diagnosis_name[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\nFor example:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diabetes[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\n\n## Patient Symptoms\nI've been having a fever for a few days now, and it's been getting worse. I'm also really itchy, and I've been throwing up. I feel really weak and tired, and my head hurts. My muscles are also really sore.\n\nPlease provide your reasoning and final diagnosis.", "prediction": "malaria", "ground_truth": "malaria", "was_correct": true, "prompt_len": 6559, "context_len": 5663, "prompt_text": "Choose the label that best fits the problem. The profiles are compact summaries\nof labeled examples; use the example wording and distinctive features to compare categories.\nUse the exact spelling of one learned label, follow any answer format explicitly requested\nin the problem, and do not add qualifications.\n\nLearned label profiles:\nLabel: allergy\nDistinctive terms: stuffy, nasal, congestion, taste, stiff\nRepresentative example: I have a stuffy nose and nasal congestion. I sometimes have a stiff neck and chest discomfort at night. I can't taste or smell anything.\n\nLabel: arthritis\nDistinctive terms: without, tight, move, around, walk\nRepresentative example: I've been having a lot of pain in my joints and my neck has been really tight. It's hard for me to move around without getting stiff and it's really painful to walk.\n\nLabel: bronchial asthma\nDistinctive terms: thick, sticky, mucous, just, dealing\nRepresentative example: I've been coughing a lot, and I'm really tired. I have a fever, and it's hard to breathe. I also cough up a lot of mucous.\n\nLabel: cervical spondylosis\nDistinctive terms: weakness, chronic, still, standing, limbs\nRepresentative example: I've been having back pain, a chronic cough, and muscle weakness. I'm also dizzy and losing my balance, and my neck hurts.\n\nLabel: chicken pox\nDistinctive terms: small, especially, eating, bumps, arms\nRepresentative example: I have red, itchy bumps all over my body. They're especially bad on my arms and legs. I also have a headache and a fever. I don't feel like eating anything and have lost my appetite.\n\nLabel: common cold\nDistinctive terms: throat, feels, sneezing, scratchy, gunk\nRepresentative example: I've been sneezing a lot, and I feel really tired. I have a lot of gunk in my nose and throat, and my throat hurts. My neck also feels swollen.\n\nLabel: dengue\nDistinctive terms: wrong, worried, what, too, sure\nRepresentative example: I have developed rashes all over my body that are itchy and I have lost my appetite. I feel very tired all day and I feel like something is wrong with my body.\n\nLabel: diabetes\nDistinctive terms: urinate, twitching, tremors, thirst, things\nRepresentative example: I have a feeling of tremors and muscle twitching. I have decreased sense of smell or taste and I feel fatigued. Sometimes I have a feeling of rapid hearbeat or palipatations. I also have a feeling of thirst and I urinate frequently.\n\nLabel: drug reaction\nDistinctive terms: often, marks, leaves, itch, flaky\nRepresentative example: I have rashes on my chest and back and I itch all over my body. I sometimes have flaky skin, which often leaves marks on my body.\n\nLabel: fungal infection\nDistinctive terms: weird, these, than, spots, rest\nRepresentative example: I have a lot of itchy spots on my skin. They're sometimes red or bumpy, and sometimes they're different colors than the rest of my skin. I also get these weird bumps that look like little balls.\n\nLabel: hypertension\nDistinctive terms: dizziness, concentrating, pains, focusing, focus\nRepresentative example: I've been having headaches, chest discomfort, dizziness, and difficulty concentrating.\n\nLabel: impetigo\nDistinctive terms: near, sores, touch, struggling, spread\nRepresentative example: I have been having a fever for a few days and now I have sores near my nose. The sores are painful and I feel uncomfortable.\n\nLabel: jaundice\nDistinctive terms: yellow, weight, turned, throwing, intense\nRepresentative example: I've been feeling really sick and tired. I've also had a fever and lost a lot of weight. My skin and urine have both turned yellow. I've also been having some stomach pain.\n\nLabel: malaria\nDistinctive terms: chills, sweating, unwell, sore, scratching\nRepresentative example: I've been feeling really sick. I have a high fever, chills, and a headache. I've also been vomiting and sweating a lot. I'm also really itchy and my muscles hurt.\n\nLabel: migraine\nDistinctive terms: vision, usually, think, sound, side\nRepresentative example: I have been having headaches for a long time. They are usually on one side of my head and are very painful. I also get nausea, vomiting, and sensitivity to light and sound.\n\nLabel: peptic ulcer disease\nDistinctive terms: use, sleep, no, nervous, keeps\nRepresentative example: I have a lot of stomach pain, and it's hard for me to sleep. I also feel really anxious and have no appetite.\n\nLabel: pneumonia\nDistinctive terms: racing, heart, cold, brown, mucus\nRepresentative example: I'm having trouble breathing and have a fever. I'm sweating a lot and feel really tired and cold. My heart is racing and I'm coughing up some brown mucus.\n\nLabel: psoriasis\nDistinctive terms: patches, scaly, problems, peeling, off\nRepresentative example: I have a skin condition that causes dry, flaky patches on my skin. I also have joint pain and the skin on my knees and elbows is peeling off.\n\nLabel: typhoid\nDistinctive terms: diarrhea, constipation, watery, vomit, stomachache\nRepresentative example: I have had diarrhea for a few days now. It is very watery and smells bad. I also have a severe headache and feel like vomiting.\n\nLabel: urinary tract infection\nDistinctive terms: pee, control, three, terrible, temps\nRepresentative example: I've had low temps and blood in my urine for the past three days. My pee smells terrible, and my head hurts so much. I can't control when I need to pee.\n\nLabel: varicose veins\nDistinctive terms: veins, self, protruding, noticeable, conscious\nRepresentative example: I have a rash on my legs that is getting worse. I have difficulty running.\n\nProblem:\nYou are an expert medical diagnostician. Based on the patient's symptoms, provide a diagnosis.\n\nPossible diagnoses include: drug reaction, allergy, chicken pox, diabetes, psoriasis, hypertension, cervical spondylosis, bronchial asthma, varicose veins, malaria, dengue, arthritis, impetigo, fungal infection, common cold, gastroesophageal reflux disease, urinary tract infection, typhoid, pneumonia, peptic ulcer disease, jaundice, migraine.\n\nPlease analyze the symptoms step by step, then provide your final diagnosis in the format:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diagnosis_name[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\nFor example:\n[DIAGNOSIS]diabetes[/DIAGNOSIS]\n\n\n## Patient Symptoms\nI've been having a fever for a few days now, and it's been getting worse. I'm also really itchy, and I've been throwing up. I feel really weak and tired, and my head hurts. My muscles are also really sore.\n\nPlease provide your reasoning and final diagnosis.\n\nReturn JSON only: {\"reasoning\": \"brief rationale\", \"final_answer\": \"exact label\"}", "trace_id": "010d82c357ac"}
